React Fiber is the new internal engine (core algorithm) of React that controls:

how React updates the UI
when rendering happens
which updates are more important
how rendering can be paused/resumed

Before Fiber, React used a simpler recursive rendering process that worked synchronously.


Problem Before Fiber

Old React rendering worked like this:

Old React Flow:

Update starts
      ↓
React renders whole component tree
      ↓
Browser gets control

While React was rendering:

browser could not do other work
animations could lag
scrolling could freeze
typing could feel slow

Because rendering was:

synchronous

meaning:

once started
React must finish everything before stopping

What Fiber Introduced

Fiber changed React rendering into:

interruptible rendering

React can now:

pause work
continue later
prioritize important updates
split big work into small chunks